WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:01.174
- You get what you wanna get.

00:00:01.174 --> 00:00:02.362
In and out.

00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:03.664
Don't have to wait in line.

00:00:03.664 --> 00:00:04.641
(whooshes and squeaks)

00:00:04.641 --> 00:00:07.141
(salsa music)

00:00:08.092 --> 00:00:10.695
- [Host] If you don't
know what a bodega is,

00:00:10.695 --> 00:00:13.281
then you probably haven't
lived in New York.

00:00:13.281 --> 00:00:17.285
In Spanish, bodega
translates to grocery store.

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:20.043
And in New York it's the
neighborhood corner store

00:00:20.043 --> 00:00:21.902
where you can get anything from beer

00:00:21.902 --> 00:00:23.051
to diapers.

00:00:23.051 --> 00:00:24.526
A new start up called Bodega,

00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:27.783
promises he same convenience
as an actual bodega

00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:31.366
but a lot of people
are not happy about it.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:35.735
So why do we need bodegas?

00:00:43.885 --> 00:00:45.119
(sizzles)

00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:46.863
- But we need bodegas because

00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:48.721
where am I gonna get my tacos?

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:50.330
- That's the beauty of bodegas,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.705
you can get tacos in one place,

00:00:52.705 --> 00:00:56.058
and something completely
different in another neighborhood.

00:00:56.058 --> 00:00:58.870
- I've been coming to
Hajji's for, I want to say

00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.790
since I was like 11.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.782
You could come here and
get anything that you need.

00:01:01.782 --> 00:01:03.525
Come here and get the chopped cheese

00:01:03.525 --> 00:01:04.579
which is what I'm getting now.

00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:07.893
Hajji's is known for it's
famous chopped cheese.

00:01:07.893 --> 00:01:10.671
We toast it, you can get
whatever kind of cheese you like.

00:01:10.671 --> 00:01:13.985
- So if I would make maybe 200
maybe 300 sandwiches a day.

00:01:13.985 --> 00:01:16.092
- Get to know the people
in the neighborhood.

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:18.065
Get to know the people that work here,

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:18.984
get to know you.

00:01:18.984 --> 00:01:20.440
- I've been working for the store

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.322
since about 20 years ago.

00:01:21.322 --> 00:01:23.486
And I have a good customer here

00:01:23.486 --> 00:01:24.348
and everybody love me.

00:01:24.348 --> 00:01:26.762
- The people work here been my friend

00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:28.199
for more than 30 years.

00:01:28.199 --> 00:01:29.526
You say you want one beer.

00:01:29.526 --> 00:01:31.072
You buy one beer.

00:01:31.072 --> 00:01:34.739
You want like a plantian,
you buy one plantain.

00:01:34.739 --> 00:01:35.784
- [Host] For many people,

00:01:35.784 --> 00:01:38.485
bodegas feel like home,
it's about the people

00:01:38.485 --> 00:01:39.568
and the cats.

00:01:42.297 --> 00:01:44.079
- We got her since she was a baby.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.358
(sizzles)

00:01:46.358 --> 00:01:48.775
- The greatest hangover food.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.397
- [Host] Each bodega,
depending on the neighborhood,

00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:54.902
has something you just
can't get anywhere else.

00:01:54.902 --> 00:01:57.152
- [Man] Those are powerful.

00:02:03.214 --> 00:02:05.214
(dings)

00:02:06.607 --> 00:02:09.768
- [Host] There are just some
things a machine can't replace.

00:02:09.768 --> 00:02:11.511
- Thanks for coming, have a good day, bye.

00:02:11.511 --> 00:02:13.928
(soft music)

00:02:17.181 --> 00:02:20.431
(whooshes and squeaks)

